-- title:
--   Chart-pinned generic fibre of the Igusa model over ℚ
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$, write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}=$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) for the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subset\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions attached to $N$, with $j=$ `jFull N` its $j$-invariant element. Assume $j$ is transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$, that $j\neq 0$, and that $F$ is finite-dimensional over each of $\mathbb{Q}(j)$ and $\mathbb{Q}(j^{-1})$. Assume further given $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra isomorphisms $e^{\mathrm{fin}}\colon \mathbb{Q}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}\mathcal{A}_0\to A_0$ and $e^{\infty}\colon \mathbb{Q}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}\mathcal{A}_\infty\to A_\infty$, where $\mathcal{A}_0=$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, $\mathcal{A}_\infty=$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ` are the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-chart algebras of the Igusa construction and $A_0=$ `CurveModel.chartRing ℚ {j}`, $A_\infty=$ `CurveModel.chartRing ℚ {j⁻¹}` are the subalgebras of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Q}[j]$, resp. $\mathbb{Q}[j^{-1}]$, together with the pinning conditions that $e^{\mathrm{fin}}(1\otimes b)=b$ and $e^{\infty}(1\otimes b)=b$ as elements of $F$. Let $M_0=$ `CurveModel.ofGenerator ℚ j htrans` be the two-chart curve model of $F/\mathbb{Q}$ built from $j$. Then there exists a morphism $e_0$ from the underlying scheme of $M_0$ to the fibre product of `igusaTo N ℓ` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}\to\mathbb{Q}$, which is an isomorphism, such that $e_0$ followed by the second projection is the structure morphism $M_0\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$, and such that on the two charts of $M_0$ the composite with the first projection to the Igusa scheme is pinned: the chart immersion `CurveModel.ι₀ ℚ j` followed by $e_0$ and the projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{A}_0\to\mathbb{Q}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}\mathcal{A}_0\xrightarrow{e^{\mathrm{fin}}}A_0$ followed by `ιFin N ℓ`, and likewise `CurveModel.ιInf ℚ j` with $e^{\infty}$ and `ιInf N ℓ`.
--
--   This identifies the generic fibre of the Igusa integral model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with the two-chart smooth proper model of the modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$, in a form pinned on both charts by the prescribed chart-ring identifications, so that the isomorphism is determined rather than merely asserted to exist abstractly. It is the $\mathbb{Q}$-level counterpart of the corresponding statement over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and is used by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_genericFibreIso_chartPin_galoisCompat_and_ratPlaceCompat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_genericFibreIso_chartPin_galoisCompat_and_ratPlaceCompat), where the Galois- and place-compatibility clauses are added.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_exists_genericFibreIso_rat_chartPin.lean

